<article class='article policies'>
    <ul class='bread'>
        <li><a href='/'>Project Essence</a></li>
        <li>Policies</li>
    </ul>
    <h1>a few quiet agreements</h1>
    <div class='article__intro'>
        <p>
            So every visit stays calm, considered, and fair to everyone in the
            room -  <div>here is what to expect, and what we ask of you.</div>
        </p>
    </div>

    <section>
        <header>
            <h4><i>01</i>Booking</h4>
            <h2>Card on File</h2>
        </header>
        <p>
            To secure a visit, every guest keeps an active credit or debit card
            on file - in line with our cancellation and no-show policies. Add
            yours online, by phone with an administrator, or in person at either
            location.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <header>
            <h4><i>02</i>Booking</h4>
            <h2>Appointment Confirmation</h2>
        </header>
        <p>
            Your visit is confirmed once you receive an "appointment accepted"
            text or email. If it doesn't arrive, please reach out.
        </p>
        <p>
            We kindly ask that every visit be reconfirmed one day ahead - via
            the reminder link or directly with an administrator. Unconfirmed
            visits may be released.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <header>
            <h4><i>03</i>Timing</h4>
            <h2>Late Arrival</h2>
        </header>
        <p>
            We plan the timing of each visit carefully, so you're cared for from
            the very first minute. Let us know as soon as you're running late
            and we'll do what we can to honour your original reservation.
        </p>
        <dl>
            <dt>Past 15 minutes</dt>
            <dd>We may simplify your service - polish-free, a natural camouflage
                base, or no design - so you're still cared for without
                disrupting the guests after you.</dd>
        </dl>

        <dl>
            <dt>Past 30 minutes</dt>
            <dd>Unfortunately we may be unable to accommodate the visit. A 50%
                cancellation fee applies and the appointment is treated as a
                no-show - this keeps things fair for our team and every other
                guest.</dd>
        </dl>
    </section>

    <section>
        <header>
            <h4><i>04</i>Booking</h4>
            <h2>24-Hour Policy</h2>
        </header>
        <p>
            Appointments cannot be rescheduled or cancelled within 24 hours of
            the start time. If we're unable to refill the slot, a late
            cancellation or no-show may be charged 50% of the reserved service
            value.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <header>
            <h4><i>05</i>During your visit</h4>
            <h2>Additional Services & Designs</h2>
        </header>
        <p>
            Nail designs and spa or healing add-ons are best booked in advance.
            Without prior notice, time constraints may mean we can't accommodate
            them the same day.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <header>
            <h4><i>06</i>Care</h4>
            <h2>Health & Safety</h2>
        </header>
        <p>
            If we suspect a condition or infection that could put you, your
            technician, or other guests at risk, we reserve the right to decline
            service - at no charge to you. Your safety always comes first.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <header>
            <h4><i>07</i>Care</h4>
            <h2>Service Guarantee</h2>
        </header>
        <p>
            We take responsibility for the quality of our work. If there's an
            issue with your nails, brows, or lashes due to our negligence, we'll
            make it right at no additional cost - within 3 days of your original
            visit.
        </p>
        <p class='article__note'>
            <b>Please note:</b>
            we do not offer a polish change without the complete manicure or
            pedicure process.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <header>
            <h4><i>08</i>Care</h4>
            <h2>Refund Policy</h2>
        </header>
        <p>
            Given the nature of our services, we do not offer refunds. We're
            committed to the highest quality of care - if something feels off,
            tell us within our guarantee period and we'll address it promptly.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <header>
            <h4><i>09</i>In the salon</h4>
            <h2>In the salon</h2>
        </header>
        <p>
            We aim to keep this a cozy, pleasant space for everyone. So that it
            stays that way, we ask guests to avoid:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Being under the influence of alcohol or drugs</li>
            <li>Food consumption in treatment areas</li>
            <li>Loud calls or videos without headphones</li>
            <li>Offensive language</li>
            <li>Guests not receiving a service - including children, friends,
                family, or pets</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <header>
            <h4><i>10</i>In the salon</h4>
            <h2>Mutual Respect</h2>
        </header>
        <p>
            We value every guest - and we're equally committed to the comfort
            and well-being of our technicians and administrators. In cases of
            inappropriate behaviour, we reserve the right to refuse further
            service.
        </p>
    </section>
</article>